Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 04:50:25 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 04/10] Vulkan FG input: every DLSS mode, fullscreen
 sub-rectangles, FG handle lifetime, recovery, unfocused FG

- Scale low-resolution FG depth/motion vectors to the output grid on the GPU
  (compute, raw texels) and convert the motion-vector scale; no permanent
  serial fallback on a size mismatch.
- Accept FG inputs whose valid regions have their own origins (fullscreen
  below monitor resolution).
- Track FG/NGX handles with generations instead of an 8-entry table.
- Rebuild the relay automatically once GPU completion is proven after a stall.
- Keep DLSS-G running while the window is visible but not focused (scoped
  Streamline focus gate), and keep DWM composing the game's monitor so
  present-mode switches no longer show frames without NR.
- Replace the Generic hash whitelist with reported compatibility problems;
  source overrides pause NR instead of stopping it until restart.
- Tests: tests/vulkan-fg-quality; trace test builds with /utf-8.
